<Article title="About DeadHangs.com: Independent Dead Hang Training Resource" description="DeadHangs.com provides free dead hang tools, training records and equipment guidance. Learn who publishes it and how claims are handled.">
<div class="article-header"><div class="article-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span>About DeadHangs.com.</div><h1 class="article-h1">About DeadHangs.com.</h1><p class="article-subtitle">DeadHangs.com is an independent resource published by Sunny Patel. It brings simple training tools and practical dead hang guidance together.</p></div>
<div class="article-body"><h2>Tools for your own practice</h2><p>The timer runs editable hang and rest intervals. The training log stores the holds you enter in your browser. The calculator compares your hold with a personal target or previous result. None of these tools provides a medical assessment.</p><p>Open the <a href="/training-log/">free timer and training log</a> without an account.</p><h2>Evidence and corrections</h2><p>We distinguish published research from personal training examples. Handgrip-force studies cannot automatically provide timed-hang percentiles. Unsupported age benchmarks and testing claims have been corrected in the relevant guides.</p><p>Our <a href="/editorial-standards/">editorial standards</a> explain the source, review and correction process. The site does not claim clinician review or professional coaching credentials for its content.</p><h2>How the site can earn</h2><p>Disclosed affiliate links may earn a commission from purchases. The free tools remain available without a purchase. Buying guides should explain fit and limitations before sending you to a retailer.</p><h2>Your training data</h2><p>The log stays in the current browser and can be exported or deleted. Analytics is optional. Email signup is also optional and separate from using the tools.</p><p>Read the <a href="/privacy/">privacy notice</a> for the actual storage and analytics behaviour.</p><h2>Contact the publisher</h2><p>Corrections, practical feedback and partnership enquiries can be sent to the publisher. Please identify the page and provide a source for factual corrections.</p><p>Open the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p></div>
</Article>
